**/static_docs/
**/.docusaurus/
wiki/transcendence/docs/
wiki/api/

# ── Dev TLS reverse-proxy configs (localhost-only) ────────────────────────
# The only Semgrep findings in these are the intentional, security-reviewed
# reverse-proxy patterns the Dockerised dev proxy REQUIRES: a server-side `set`
# upstream resolved lazily via `resolver` (so the proxy still boots when an
# upstream container is down/restarting), and Host / X-Forwarded-Host forwarding
# for upstream vhost routing. Both are safe on a loopback-only TLS front door and
# are annotated inline with `# nosemgrep` + rationale. They are excluded here
# because GitHub code-scanning surfaces in-source nosemgrep suppressions
# (suppressions.kind = "inSource") as OPEN alerts rather than honoring them.
# nginx syntax is gated separately by `nginx -t`.
infrastructure/tls/nginx.conf
infrastructure/scripts/tls/nginx.conf
